{"ts":"2026-09-21T00:14:00Z","event":"issue","plan":"260920-zqapye-installable-harness","phase":2,"task":"TASK-010","message":"cannot verify by hand tonight whether Claude Code reads ~/.claude/commands/ globally (no live session available, per explicit user instruction). DECISION: install both skills and commands at global scope by default (the full feature), rather than pre-emptively narrowing to skills-only. Rationale: if the assumption is false, the cost is an inert file sitting in ~/.claude/commands/, fully recoverable by `pinst harness uninstall`; if the assumption were wrongly assumed false and skills-only shipped, a working feature would be silently withheld with no way for a user to know they were missing it. The asymmetry favors installing everything. ASSUMPTION-002 stays open in README.md Open Questions for a human to confirm later; nothing downstream depends on the answer either way, exactly as the plan anticipated.","detail":{}}
